The doxygen help page of 'gradient' should lead to the example
https://github.com/kaskr/adcomp/blob/92c59970843c03488e7d5fdca053ec795eba3f5d/tmb_examples/laplace.cpp#L38-L86
which is fairly close to what you are trying to do in your struct 'func'.
The func evaluation operator needs to apply the conversions, something like:

    T zeta1 = T(this->zeta1); // constant
    T h1 = theta(0); // variable
    T h2 = theta(1); // variable
    vector<T> Qpartition = this->Qpartition.template cast<T>(); // constant

etc., to mention a few of them.

As an unrelated comment, your code could be greatly simplified and generalized (e.g. using cumsum?). And you should be aware of the effect of parameter dependent branching, which may or may not be an issue in your case.

